# Copy to `pipeline/.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored — never commit real values.
#
# Everything except `translate` and `publish` runs with this file empty or absent:
# scrape / images / build / verify / verify-images need no credentials at all.

# --- translate -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Only `holo-data translate` needs this. Get a key from https://poe.com/api_key
POE_API_KEY=your_api_key_here

# --- publish -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Only `holo-data publish` needs these, and only the maintainer can publish.
# Also run: uv sync --extra publish
#
# Create the token at: Cloudflare dashboard → R2 → Manage API Tokens → Create token
#   Permission: Object Read & Write
#   Scope:      *only* the two buckets named in apps/api/wrangler.jsonc
#               (hololive-ocg-wiki-images, hololive-ocg-wiki-artifacts)
#
# Scoping to those two buckets is deliberate: the CLI may be driven by an agent (D4), and
# a token that cannot reach any other bucket bounds the damage structurally rather than
# by carefulness. See docs/infra.md for the full setup.

# Not a secret — it appears in every R2 endpoint URL. Kept here for symmetry.
R2_ACCOUNT_ID=
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# Optional. Bucket names come from apps/api/wrangler.jsonc; these override for a one-off
# (e.g. publishing to a scratch bucket). Leave unset in normal use.
# R2_IMAGES_BUCKET=
# R2_ARTIFACTS_BUCKET=
